# ==============================================================================
# LIFE SHARE: Deployment Architecture & Fixes Audit
# ==============================================================================
#
# PROBLEM: The frontend on Netlify tries to call http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1
# which is unreachable from the public internet.
#
# SOLUTION ARCHITECTURE:
#
#   User → Netlify (frontend) → Production Backend URL → Database
#
# STEPS:
# 1. Set VITE_API_URL in Netlify environment variables to point to deployed backend
# 2. Backend must be deployed to a service like Render, Railway, Fly.io, etc.
# 3. Backend CORS must include the Netlify domain
# 4. The backend already has allow_origin_regex for *.netlify.app ✓
#
# For local development, this .env is used:
VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1
